---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'The Coherence Co. | Accelerate With Alignment',
  description: 'Because alignment is the strategy.',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <div class="design-note">Design Mockup — Updated Brief — March 2026</div>

  <section class="hero-home">
    <div class="container-home hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-left">
        <span class="hero-tagline">For C-Suite Executives & Senior Leaders</span>
        <h1 class="hero-title">Accelerate With Alignment</h1>
        <p class="hero-sub-title">Because alignment is the strategy.</p>
        <p class="hero-body">
          When execution outpaces comprehension, you lose collaboration. The Coherence Protocol helps leadership teams align narrative, pace, and trust — so you can build momentum without leaving your people and their best ideas behind.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Get Your Coherence Score</a>
          <a href="/coherence-canvas" class="btn-ghost">See The Framework →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-right">
        {[
          { num: '21', label: 'Innovation Yield Recovery' },
          { num: '47', label: 'Decision-Making Velocity' },
          { num: '35', label: 'Coherence Index Improvement' }
        ].map((stat) => (
          <div class="hero-credential">
            <div class="credential-num">{stat.num}<span>%</span></div>
            <div class="credential-label">
              <strong>{stat.label}</strong> with the Coherence Protocol
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-pain">
    <div class="container-home">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="eyebrow">What Velocity Strain Is Costing You</span>
        <div class="section-rule"></div>
        <h2 class="section-title">Your Team Is Paying the Price</h2>
        <p class="section-sub">Leadership systems rarely fail because leaders lack commitment. They struggle when signals, interpretation, and decision velocity drift out of alignment under pressure.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pain-grid">
        <div class="pain-card">
          <span class="pain-num">01</span>
          <h3 class="pain-title">Your Calendar Owns You</h3>
          <p class="pain-body">You're triple-booked. Every meeting bleeds into the next. Your team sees a leader who's always "on" but never fully present. They're not making decisions, so timelines are slipping.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pain-card">
          <span class="pain-num">02</span>
          <h3 class="pain-title">Your Strategy Exists Only in Your Head</h3>
          <p class="pain-body">You know where the company is going. Your exec team thinks they know. The VP layer has three different interpretations. Your $2M initiative is executing against a story you never told.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pain-card">
          <span class="pain-num">03</span>
          <h3 class="pain-title">You're Losing Your Best People</h3>
          <p class="pain-body">Your top performers don't quit because of comp. They quit because they can't make sense of the whiplash. Priorities change weekly. Strategic clarity lasts 72 hours.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-content">
    <div class="container-home">
      <div class="content-grid">
        <div class="content-left">
          <span class="eyebrow">The Variable You're Missing</span>
          <div class="section-rule"></div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Most Executive Teams Are Optimizing the Wrong Variable</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="content-right">
          <p>You're measuring speed: number of deals closed, number of features launched, number of decisions made in a week. That's industrial thinking applied to knowledge work.</p>
          <div class="pullquote">The executives who win the next decade aren't the fastest. They are the most coherent.</div>
          <p>They've learned that velocity without integration creates debt. Not financial debt. Narrative debt. Trust debt. Attention debt.</p>
          <p>The Coherence Protocol is built on a different assumption: sustainable performance isn't about moving faster. It's about moving at the speed your system can absorb change without fragmenting.</p>
          <p style="font-style:italic; color:var(--navy); font-weight:500">This isn't therapy. It's engineering for executive attention.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-faqs">
    <div class="container-home">
      <div class="faqs-grid">
        <div class="faqs-left">
          <span class="eyebrow">Common Questions</span>
          <div class="section-rule"></div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Most leaders ask these before deciding.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          {[
            { q: 'What does "Coherence" actually mean?', a: 'Coherence is the measurable alignment between what an organization says, what it decides, and what it actually does — under load, over time, and across layers of authority.' },
            { q: 'How is this different from coaching?', a: 'Traditional executive coaching focuses on individual skill-building. The Coherence Protocol diagnoses where your organization’s system is failing its people.' },
            { q: 'How long until we see results?', a: 'Immediate: The Coherence Assessment shows your baseline. Medium-term (30 days): Measurable coherence index improvement.' }
          ].map((item) => (
            <div class="faq-item">
              <p class="faq-q">{item.q}</p>
              <p class="faq-a">{item.a}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  :root {
    --navy: #13294B;
    --gold: #C4922A;
    --limestone: #F0EDE8;
    --warm-white: #FAF8F5;
    --warm-white-2: #F5F2EC;
    --muted: #6B7A8D;
    --divider: rgba(19, 41, 75, 0.12);
    --serif: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    --sans: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
  }

  .container-home { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 2.5rem; }
  .eyebrow { display: block; font-size: 0.6rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .section-rule { width: 40px; height: 2px; background: var(--gold); margin-bottom: 2rem; }

  /* Hero */
  .hero-home { background: var(--limestone); padding: 120px 0 100px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider); }
  .hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 6rem; align-items: end; }
  .hero-title { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 4rem); font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--navy); line-height: 1.05; }
  .hero-sub-title { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.4rem; font-style: italic; color: #1d3a5c; margin: 1rem 0 2.5rem; }
  .hero-body { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.85; max-width: 420px; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  
  /* Stats */
  .hero-credential { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.25rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--divider); }
  .credential-num { font-size: 2.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy); min-width: 80px; }
  .credential-num span { font-size: 0.7rem; color: var(--gold); vertical-align: super; }
  .credential-label strong { display: block; font-size: 0.65rem; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }

  /* Pain Grid */
  .section-pain { background: var(--warm-white); padding: 100px 0; }
  .pain-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); border: 1px solid var(--divider); }
  .pain-card { padding: 2.5rem; background: white; border-right: 1px solid var(--divider); }
  .pain-card:last-child { border-right: none; }
  .pain-title { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 1rem; }

  /* Content */
  .section-content { background: var(--warm-white-2); padding: 100px 0; }
  .content-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.5fr; gap: 6rem; }
  .pullquote { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.2rem; font-style: italic; color: var(--navy); border-left: 3px solid var(--gold); padding: 1rem 1.5rem; background: white; margin: 2rem 0; }

  /* FAQ */
  .section-faqs { background: var(--warm-white); padding: 100px 0; }
  .faqs-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.8fr; gap: 6rem; }
  .faq-item { padding: 1.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--divider); }
  .faq-q { font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }

  /* Buttons */
  .btn-primary { background: var(--navy); color: white; padding: 0.9rem 1.75rem; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.65rem; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; }
  .btn-ghost { color: var(--navy); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--navy); font-size: 0.65rem; font-weight: 700; margin-left: 1.5rem; }
  .design-note { background: var(--gold); color: white; text-align: center; padding: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .hero-grid, .pain-grid, .content-grid, .faqs-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 3rem; }
  }
</style>